{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01NWEPvNQCArKxmYRGpJs5ij","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Anchor** is a single-user personal productivity system for J.C. Liechty, living entirely in `C:\\dev\\Anchor` (no syncing, no siblings, plain-text source of truth).\n\n- **What it is at the core:** a GTD-style task/project manager backed by **plain markdown files** (`DASHBOARD.md`, `PROJECTS.md`, `INBOX.md`, `domains/*.md`, plus cancelled/saved archives). The markdown is the source of truth â€” no database, no binary formats.\n\n- **What it ships as the application:** `anchor_gui.py`, a self-contained **Python-stdlib HTTP server + browser dashboard** bound to `http://localhost:8777`, run persistently as the NSSM Windows service `anchor`. It reads/writes the markdown directly through a local API (done/add/capture/cancel/save/restore, task & project editing, priority promote/demote).\n\n- **CLI mirror:** `anchor.py` reproduces the same logic as a command-line tool and generates the static `dashboard.html`. It mirrors the GUI's task ops and the R&D inspection seams.\n\n- **Self-test harness:** `anchor_healthcheck.py` runs daily at 5 AM (Task Scheduler), parsing every markdown file, booting a throwaway server, exercising every endpoint and task-state transition, walking the v2/v3/v4 R&D surfaces fully stubbed, and writing `health_reports/YYYY-MM-DD.md`.\n\n- **Its major evolving feature â€” the R&D control surface (v2â†’v3â†’v4):** turns each project's window into a **\"Project Cockpit\"** for trio-driven R&D (researchPrime â†’ Crucible â†’ Foreman). It manages **sessions** (one trio run = one session), proactive **cached/validated summaries**, a **Grass Catchers** idea lane, and **type-aware deliverables**.\n\n- **The v3/v4 terminal substrate:** real interactive **ConPTY terminals** (xterm.js over a hand-rolled WebSocket / SSE fallback), each isolated in its own **git worktree + branch**, with a durable session registry, status-light lanes, inline expanding panels, an engine toggle (Claudeâ†”Gemini), per-lane doc roles, and a cost/tokens/time rollup.\n\n- **Notable constraint it lives by:** **Python stdlib only**, with exactly one declared exception â€” the optional `pywinpty` for the terminal subsystem (lazy import, `pip install .[terminal]`, degrades gracefully if absent). `distro.py` enforces this by refusing any other native/third-party import in product code.\n\n- **Branding:** presented as a **Ghost World Labs** tool \"powered by NextGen Nuclear â˜¢\" (vendored brand mark serves as favicon and masthead lockup).\n\nIn short: a markdown-backed personal task manager that has grown a sophisticated, locally-served mission-control layer for orchestrating AI research/planning/build agents per project."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4412,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":45093,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"07af89e5-91f7-4a27-851d-28ca78992f52","uuid":"266970fb-21d3-42e4-949f-9437fc7f01a7","request_id":"req_011Cc1H6fkrmVijmkYbBTj7H"}
